In Kubernetes, a Volume is a storage mechanism that allows containers in a Pod to store and share data.

Volume Types Commonly Used in Real Projects

PersistentVolume (PV) – Represents persistent storage.
PersistentVolumeClaim (PVC) – Pods request storage through PVCs.
StorageClass – Dynamically provisions storage (e.g., AWS EBS gp3).
ConfigMap – Stores application configuration.
Secret – Stores passwords, API keys, and certificates.
emptyDir – Temporary storage shared within a Pod.
CSI Volumes – Integrates Kubernetes with cloud storage (AWS EBS/EFS, Azure Disk, GCP PD, IBM Block/File Storage).
NFS or EFS – Shared file storage when multiple Pods need concurrent access.
